B. Prototype Applications

Two prototypes were developed with similar on-location marker-based AR features ( Figure 1 ), but with a different UX design. This decision was made to test the effectiveness of location-based navigation in a modified UI to better complement AR features. UX1 only had a static map and buttons at the bottom ( Figure 2 ), with a location driven UI implemented in UX2 ( Figure 3 , Figure 4 ). In both applications, the user simply points the smartphone to a target using the camera. Information about Valletta is given through text, images, video and 3D models, with the user answering a question about the point of interest. Game points are added or subtracted according to the user responses. The applications were developed with Unity 3 as game engine, Vuforia for AR 4 , MapBox 5 for location-based game features and Maya for 3D modelling 6 .
