2) Readiness to use the AR application:

Following a demonstration of the AR application, 41% answered positively in readiness to use the AR application, while 52% were indecisive. Only 7% answered negatively. On further analysis employing a correlation test, respondents not ready to use the AR application, also view AR as difficult to use, signifying that proficiency is a factor that impacts readiness.
B. Pre-Post Test Interviews

The six participants were interviewed prior to using the application. After choosing a device, the participants toured the city via the treasure-hunt game. Following the walk-around, participants recounted their experience. Data tracking each user’s behaviour was collected in real-time within the application and automatically exported, upon completion of the tour. Pre-post test interviews and device data logs were analysed first separately and than triangulated. For this purpose, the six participants were randomly assigned codes from RP1 to RP6. RP1-RP4 chose UX1 (Live Map version) and RP5-RP6 (static map).
C. Tracking Data Analysis and Triangulation with Interviews

Tracking data analysis was conducted with all participants. Figure 6 depicts an example of our analysis using RP1’s GPS track report, which is consistent with the technique employed with other participants. This data is generated from different co-ordinates during logging, which then formed a track of the pathway the user went through to reach the markers to finish the game.

RP1’s total time to complete the tour was of 13 minutes (4 minutes in motion & 9 minutes idle), with a total distance of 1.03km and average speed of 4.93km/h. Figures 7 and 8 show the speed (y-axis) along the route distance(x-axis). RP1 spent most of the time in idle when stopping to locate the marker and answer the question next to the point of interest. Given that participant was familiar with the streets of Valletta, RP1 moved with ease between venues. The location where RP1 took the most time was next to St. John’s Co-Cathedral. The place where RP1 was walking fast was from Manoel Theatre to Sette Giugno Monument. A similar analysis was performed for all six participants.
